{title: O Come, O Come, Emmanuel}
{title_ko: 곧 오소서 임마누엘}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 104장}
{artist: Traditional Latin hymn / John Mason Neale}
{genre: Christmas}
{flow: Meditative}
{style: Carol}
{key: Em}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}
{score: o-come-o-come-emmanuel.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
O [Em]come, O come, Em[G]manuel
And [Em]ransom captive [D]Is[Em]rael
That [Em]mourns in lonely [G]exile here
Un[Em]til the Son of [D]God ap[Em]pear
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Re[G]joice! Re[D]joice! Em[Em]manuel
Shall [Em]come to thee, O [D]Is[Em]rael
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
O [Em]come, Thou Wisdom [G]from on high
Who [Em]orderest all [D]things mightily
To [Em]us the path of [G]knowledge show
And [Em]teach us in her [D]ways to [Em]go
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
O [Em]come, O come, Thou [G]Lord of might
Who [Em]to Thy tribes on [D]Sinai's height
In [Em]ancient times didst [G]give the law
In [Em]cloud and majesty and [D]awe[Em]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
O [Em]come, Thou Rod of [G]Jesse, free
Thine [Em]own from Satan's [D]tyranny
From [Em]depths of hell Thy [G]people save
And [Em]give them victory [D]o'er the [Em]grave
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
